# gcc skills exposed to Codex, one name per line, symlinked by install.sh:
#   ~/.agents/skills/<name> -> ~/.claude/skills/<name>
#
# Curated on purpose. Codex budgets its skills list at 2% of the context window
# (about 5k characters on gpt-6-astra) and shortens descriptions past that, so a
# blanket symlink of all 70+ gcc skills would make every skill invisible.
# Excluded by design: any skill whose value is `context: fork` (bloop, magi,
# skeptical-review, arch-qa ...), skills that drive Claude-only tools
# (AskUserQuestion, mcp__inputs, Task tool), and core-dump/catchup, whose
# codex-side equivalent is adapters/codex/skills/core-dump.
# Add a line, re-run install.sh. Remove a line, re-run; the stale link is pruned.
gcc-proposal
ipc
pin-for-dream
probe
cleanup-comments
ste-writing
pr-description
write-docs
callouts
test
